  },
  "plans": [
    {
      "planRef": "plan_1",
      "blueprint": {
        "schemaVersion": 2,
        "strategy": {
          "policy": "EXAM",
          "outcome": "Explain and use Ohm's law for one simple series circuit. Stop once I can solve and explain one changed circuit independently.",
          "explanation": "The accepted outcome is a single bounded performance: solve and explain one changed simple series circuit. No assessment date, weight or prior evidence is supplied, so I treat this as a compact conceptual-plus-procedural task rather than a full electricity course. One integrated activity teaches the needed constructs (voltage, current, resistance, series current equality, voltage drops, V=IR) and immediately applies them to a worked example, then to a changed circuit solved independently. A second activity is not committed because the integrated task already supplies explanation, supported application and independent changed example; further practice is optional or triggered only by an observed failure. The scope node is INCLUDED because it is exactly the accepted outcome; no other scope exists to defer or exclude.",
