            "localId": "changed_circuits",
            "outcomeRefs": [
              "select"
            ],
            "scopeRefs": [
              "scope_1"
            ],
            "title": "Select and solve on changed unfamiliar circuits",
            "activityType": "Independent method-selection practice",
            "purpose": "Demonstrate the accepted capability on circuits the learner has not seen, without assistance.",
            "instructions": "Take four unfamiliar circuits that are not the ones from the repertoire activity. For each: (1) state the method you will use and give a valid reason based on the circuit's topology and source types; (2) solve it completely; (3) verify the result by a second method or by checking KVL/KCL and power balance. Do not look at worked solutions until you have committed to a method and a solution. If a circuit requires a method you have not been taught, write 'gap: <method>' and move on rather than guessing. At the end, write two or three sentences on which circuit features most reliably determined your method choice and where you were still unsure.",
            "completionCriterion": "Four changed circuits each with a named method, a valid selection reason, a correct solution, and an independent check; any untaught-method gaps recorded honestly.",
            "effort": {
              "lowMinutes": 45,
              "likelyMinutes": 60,
              "highMinutes": 90
            },
            "timeboxMinutes": 60,
            "commitment": {
              "category": "COMMITTED"
            },
            "hardDependencies": [
              "method_repertoire"
            ]
          },
          {
            "localId": "targeted_remediation",
            "outcomeRefs": [
              "select"
            ],
            "scopeRefs": [
              "scope_1"
            ],
            "title": "Targeted remediation on observed selection errors",
            "activityType": "Failure-triggered remediation",
            "purpose": "Repair a specific method-selection error only if the independent practice actually reveals one.",
            "instructions": "If, and only if, the changed-circuits activity shows a wrong method choice or an incorrect solution, rework that specific circuit type: write the decision rule you missed, solve two fresh circuits of that type, and check each. If no error occurred, do not do this activity.",
            "completionCriterion": "The specific error type is corrected on two fresh circuits with correct method choice, valid reason, and checked solutions.",
            "effort": {
              "lowMinutes": 20,
              "likelyMinutes": 30,
              "highMinutes": 45
            },
            "timeboxMinutes": 30,
            "commitment": {
              "category": "CONTINGENT",
              "trigger": {
                "checkpointActivityId": "changed_circuits",
                "condition": "At least one changed circuit was solved with a wrong method choice or an incorrect final answer."
              }
            },
            "hardDependencies": [
              "changed_circuits"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "decisions": {
          "assumptions": [
            "The learner has already been taught the standard circuit analysis methods (series/parallel reduction, dividers, nodal, mesh, superposition, source transformation, Thevenin/Norton); the plan does not introduce methods beyond that repertoire.",
            "No assessment weights, past papers, or error logs were supplied, so the plan targets the accepted capability directly rather than a specific exam paper."
          ],
          "tradeOffs": [
            "No separate conceptual re-teaching of voltage and current is included, because the learner reports understanding them; effort is concentrated on selection and application.",
            "No timed exam simulation is included, because no deadline or paper format was supplied; this can be added later if an assessment is confirmed."
          ],
          "unresolvedUncertainty": [
            "The learner's actual current selection accuracy is unknown; the first activity embeds a diagnostic rather than assuming beginner status.",
            "Whether the learner has been taught every method needed for the changed circuits is unknown; untaught-method gaps are recorded honestly rather than guessed."
          ],
          "stoppingConditions": [
            "Stop when the learner can select, justify, and correctly solve unfamiliar circuits without assistance; the contingent remediation is the only extension and only fires on an observed error."
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "sharedDependencies": [],
  "tradeOffExplanation": "The plan deliberately omits re-teaching voltage and current concepts and omits timed exam practice, because the accepted outcome is method selection on unfamiliar circuits and no assessment format or deadline was supplied. Effort is concentrated on a compact decision repertoire plus independent changed-circuit practice, with remediation kept contingent on an actual observed selection error rather than added as compulsory work. This keeps the total small and finishes early within the available capacity."
}

